00:27:06.606 --> 00:27:09.947
Kirk, could diversity take away

00:27:09.947 --> 00:27:12.364
from your creativity as well?

00:27:13.325 --> 00:27:16.286
Could diversity take away
from your creativity as well?

00:27:16.286 --> 00:27:17.835
From Kirk.

00:27:17.835 --> 00:27:21.918
- Hi Kirk, I think the critical thing is

00:27:21.918 --> 00:27:23.329
stay true to your idea.

00:27:23.329 --> 00:27:25.499
Stay true to your mission, your purpose.

00:27:25.499 --> 00:27:28.197
That's fundamental,
that's your foundation.

00:27:28.197 --> 00:27:31.050
But within that, then the next question is

00:27:31.050 --> 00:27:33.316
how do you reach your audience?

00:27:33.316 --> 00:27:35.268
Then also how do you do it?

00:27:35.268 --> 00:27:36.536
How do you go to market?

00:27:36.536 --> 00:27:38.584
How do you create the product?

00:27:38.584 --> 00:27:42.485
I think by including diversity,
you actually increase

00:27:42.485 --> 00:27:45.288
the level of creativity dramatically.

00:27:45.288 --> 00:27:48.068
The financial results of
companies that are strong

00:27:48.068 --> 00:27:51.272
and diverse tend to be
way better than those

00:27:51.272 --> 00:27:55.319
that are very restrictive,
and traditional.

00:27:55.319 --> 00:27:58.092
Now I think why does
it increase diversity?

00:27:58.092 --> 00:28:01.696
If, again at Spotify,
it's really cool to have,

00:28:01.696 --> 00:28:03.438
they have this music room.

00:28:03.438 --> 00:28:06.583
Then they have this area
where they can watch people

00:28:06.583 --> 00:28:09.192
on focus groups and stuff like that.

00:28:09.192 --> 00:28:11.594
They deliberately will
get very diverse people

00:28:11.594 --> 00:28:13.896
listening to their new products,

00:28:13.896 --> 00:28:15.885
and naturally going
through the whole usability

00:28:15.885 --> 00:28:17.293
of their new products.

00:28:17.293 --> 00:28:21.533
You, 'cause I guess I've live
in technology a long time,

00:28:21.533 --> 00:28:25.700
you cannot believe how great
engineers don't realize

00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:29.482
how difficult to use their products are.

00:28:29.482 --> 00:28:31.971
They might have built the
best mousetrap in the world.

00:28:31.971 --> 00:28:34.175
They might have built the
best features or functions

00:28:34.175 --> 00:28:36.930
of the coolest kind of
music download in the world

00:28:36.930 --> 00:28:41.049
but unless it's usable
and simple, and intuitive,

00:28:41.049 --> 00:28:44.670
then it's not going to get the air time.

00:28:44.670 --> 00:28:48.837
So you never ever, ever
get disappointed by getting

00:28:51.646 --> 00:28:56.092
user feedback in terms of
road testing your products.

00:28:56.092 --> 00:28:58.692
I think around that, you
don't want to just road test

00:28:58.692 --> 00:29:00.713
unless you got a very narrow product.

00:29:00.713 --> 00:29:02.969
Just the one segment of society.

00:29:02.969 --> 00:29:05.893
It's much better if you really
want to scale your product.

00:29:05.893 --> 00:29:09.517
To do that, and then go
out to other segments

00:29:09.517 --> 00:29:11.527
and be very diverse in your thinking.

00:29:11.527 --> 00:29:14.979
I think the creativity, just
speaking for me personally,

00:29:14.979 --> 00:29:18.594
by having a lot of
people within the company

00:29:18.594 --> 00:29:22.025
challenge me from very diverse backgrounds

00:29:22.025 --> 00:29:24.690
gives me a much greater appreciation of

00:29:24.690 --> 00:29:26.716
how to do the best for our customers.

00:29:26.716 --> 00:29:29.886
So, and again, it's so true in life.

00:29:29.886 --> 00:29:32.690
Sometimes I think as an
entrepreneur, you get a bit

00:29:32.690 --> 00:29:36.347
successful, you start
believing your own PR,

00:29:36.347 --> 00:29:37.795
and you get a bit comfortable.

00:29:37.795 --> 00:29:41.086
When you do that, you kind
of lose your creativity.

00:29:41.086 --> 00:29:43.841
Whereas what your
question's all about Kirk,

00:29:43.841 --> 00:29:47.314
is about how do you
accelerate that creativity?

00:29:47.314 --> 00:29:49.510
Now I think diversity
is just one of the ways

00:29:49.510 --> 00:29:53.557
you can do that and get
some fantastic input.

00:29:53.557 --> 00:29:57.130
So really strong invention innovation.

00:29:57.130 --> 00:29:59.495
Then as a leader, you kind
of got to make the choices,

00:29:59.495 --> 00:30:03.297
and start executing, and
delivering on that vision.

00:30:03.297 --> 00:30:06.138
- Yeah, I'm definitely
with Stephen on this one.

00:30:06.138 --> 00:30:08.370
I don't know that we just
really disagree a lot

00:30:08.370 --> 00:30:09.370
though on the questions anyway.

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:12.149
Just different sides of
the coin on most of these.

00:30:12.149 --> 00:30:15.246
I don't see a world in
which for any company

00:30:15.246 --> 00:30:18.854
adding diversity would
take away from creativity.

00:30:18.854 --> 00:30:21.083
It just, I don't know how that happens.

00:30:21.083 --> 00:30:25.705
I think maybe your own, if
you're injecting other people

00:30:25.705 --> 00:30:29.127
into a company then maybe
the responsibility on you

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:31.393
isn't as great to be creative.

00:30:31.393 --> 00:30:34.298
If you have to come up with everything

00:30:34.298 --> 00:30:36.089
then now that you have
people who you can rely on,

00:30:36.089 --> 00:30:37.993
maybe you don't have to
come up with as many ideas.

00:30:37.993 --> 00:30:40.772
Maybe your own personal creativity.

00:30:40.772 --> 00:30:42.233
I don't know if that's
what he's getting at

00:30:42.233 --> 00:30:44.597
but you know, look at
what's in the best interest

00:30:44.597 --> 00:30:45.858
of your company.

00:30:45.858 --> 00:30:48.100
The best idea is when?

00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:49.963
If it's only you coming up with ideas,

00:30:49.963 --> 00:30:53.659
and the ideas are just
okay by adding more people

00:30:53.659 --> 00:30:55.376
into the mix, they can take that okay idea

00:30:55.376 --> 00:30:56.793
into a great one.

00:30:57.998 --> 00:31:00.788
So if that means you're not
coming up with every single

00:31:00.788 --> 00:31:02.982
idea for the business,
maybe that's a good thing

00:31:02.982 --> 00:31:06.312
to help you get to where you need to go.

00:31:06.312 --> 00:31:08.395
I don't know, that's just
my take on the question.

00:31:08.395 --> 00:31:11.725
- I think Evan, you probably
got some very strong

00:31:11.725 --> 00:31:13.783
fantastic experience in this area.

00:31:13.783 --> 00:31:15.829
But you need different types of input

00:31:15.829 --> 00:31:18.315
at different stages of kind
of the whole life cycle

00:31:18.315 --> 00:31:19.892
of building your product.

00:31:19.892 --> 00:31:21.644
You need to take your idea out.

00:31:21.644 --> 00:31:23.106
It's quite often I come in.

00:31:23.106 --> 00:31:25.618
I think I've got an idea,
and there's a group of people

00:31:25.618 --> 00:31:27.802
I want to kind of run it past.

00:31:27.802 --> 00:31:30.337
Actually the more diverse they
are, the more they challenge

00:31:30.337 --> 00:31:34.188
me to refine the idea to
something that can work.

00:31:34.188 --> 00:31:37.018
Then obviously the next
stage, you need to take

00:31:37.018 --> 00:31:40.480
the dreamers and allow
them to keep dreaming.

00:31:40.480 --> 00:31:42.761
Take the executors.

00:31:42.761 --> 00:31:45.673
If you're just your own
person as an entrepreneur,

00:31:45.673 --> 00:31:48.637
and you're in a micro
business and a small business

00:31:48.637 --> 00:31:52.159
and it's just you, you need to
play lots of different roles.

00:31:52.159 --> 00:31:54.158
So you know you've got the
idea, then you need to say

00:31:54.158 --> 00:31:56.450
how do I get to the network?

00:31:56.450 --> 00:31:57.902
Who do I need to sell it to?

00:31:57.902 --> 00:31:58.815
Who is the audience?

00:31:58.815 --> 00:32:00.173
How do I build the product?

00:32:00.173 --> 00:32:03.315
All these sort of things,
and all of a sudden,

00:32:03.315 --> 00:32:05.362
then once you've got the idea,

00:32:05.362 --> 00:32:07.738
you're actually selling
the product out there,

00:32:07.738 --> 00:32:10.824
it's all about execution, scaling up.

00:32:10.824 --> 00:32:12.822
Hiring great people,
all the sort of things

00:32:12.822 --> 00:32:15.284
we talked about on previous shows.

00:32:15.284 --> 00:32:19.284
I think it does change
but as you group a number

00:32:20.231 --> 00:32:23.316
